# K02 witness (next_core_tasks_v2.md K02, bullet 3; defects.md MERGE-HIDDEN-INPUT-PROJECTION):
# a merge result reaching a callee as an ordinary hidden input, with caller priority.
# `copy` is a unit-level merge result (value 1).  `read` names the free `copy\value`; `caller`
# declares its OWN `copy: merge: Other` (value 22) and calls read.  By the general hidden-input
# priority the caller's local must win: the answer is 22, not the unit-level 1.
# Today both runs exit 81 -- the global result-name lookup bypasses the dynamic input.
# Success is 7.
Model: (int: value 1)
Other: (int: value 22)
copy: merge: Model
fn: read () int
return: copy\value
fn: caller () int
    copy: merge: Other
    return: read()
end: caller
int: result caller()
if: result != 22
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 81; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
